// The TLS 1.2 server of the native backends' TLS (std/native/llrt/
// tls12srv.xo, decision 0202) against crypto/tls's client, through
// internal.crypto_op("tls12.server"), whose Go reference (std/rt
// internal_tls12.go) drives crypto/tls's server over the same bytes. The
// traces are tls12_client's (crypto/tls's client and server with random
// sources repeating 0x11 and 0x22, so the server's random, ECDHE keys,
// and RSA-PSS salts are fixed and the Xo server is given the same). The
// RSA-PSS traces are signed by the Xo server itself; crypto/tls's ECDSA
// nonces cannot be repeated, so those traces hand the server the trace's
// signature, and a masked case checks a signature it makes. Then PKCS
// #1 v1.5 (a ClientHello offering only it), the server's choices
// (suite, curve, ALPN) failing, a corrupted ClientKeyExchange and
// Finished, a client's alert, and bytes that are not TLS.
use std/internal

const CERT_P256: Str = ""
const CERT_P384: Str = ""
const KEY_P256_D: Str = "9f21bbe70040d0bb7340fd3894b1390a7fc575741aa8ff9bb82c754c6fcef8b0"
